The pure verifier proves that -D is fundamental, every displayed primitive
positive-definite form has discriminant -D and exact order five, and the
five classes have no nonzero F_5 relation.  The meet-in-the-middle halves
have 25 and 125 distinct reduced forms and meet only at the principal class.

